.TH SAVETOA 1 "September 2026" "savetoa 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
savetoa \- job-driven backup orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B savetoa
.RI [ \-\-config " path" ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B savetoa
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
SaveToA coordinates named backup targets. A target selects a capture driver,
source settings and credentials, transformations, destinations, and retention
policy.
.PP
This release is an implementation scaffold. Commands that would capture,
delete, verify, or restore data fail explicitly until implemented.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Read configuration from
.I path
instead of
.IR /etc/savetoa/config.yml .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " target"
Capture and deliver one configured target.
.TP
.BI run-group " group"
Run a configured group of targets.
.TP
.B list
List completed backup sets.
.TP
.BI verify " backup-id"
Verify a completed backup set.
.TP
.BI restore " backup-id"
Materialize a backup into an explicit restore destination.
.TP
.BI prune " target"
Apply the configured retention policy to completed backup sets.
.TP
.BI doctor " target"
Validate a target and its dependencies without capturing data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/config.yml
System-wide target configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/credentials.d/
Protected source and destination credential files.
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/recipients.d/
Client-side encryption recipients.
.TP
.I /var/lib/savetoa/
Persistent state, work directories, and delivery spool.
.TP
.I /var/backups/savetoa/
Default local backup destination.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/bionicman/savetoa/issues.
